---
import contact from '../data/contact.json';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy notice" description="How Access:Hull collects, uses and protects your personal information, and your rights under UK GDPR.">

  <section class="ah-sec" aria-labelledby="pr-h"><div class="ah-in lg-wrap">
    <nav class="lg-nav" aria-label="Policies"><a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility statement</a><a href="/privacy/" aria-current="page">Privacy notice</a><a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a><a href="/terms/">Terms of use</a></nav>
    <article class="lg">
      <p class="ah-eyebrow">Policies</p>
      <h1 id="pr-h">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="lg-up">Last updated 2 October 2026</p>
      <p class="lg-lead">This notice explains what personal information Access:Hull collects through this website, why we collect it, and your rights over it.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Access:Hull Digital Inclusion Programme is run by <span class="ph">[legal name of the organisation]</span>, <span class="ph">[registered address]</span>. We are the data controller for the information you give us. Our registration number with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) is <span class="ph">[ICO registration number]</span>.</p>
      <p>Our data protection contact is <span class="ph">[name or role]</span>, {contact.email}, {contact.phone}.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <div class="tscroll"><table class="lg-t">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">When you</th><th scope="col">We collect</th><th scope="col">Why</th><th scope="col">Lawful basis</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Fill in the partner questionnaire</td><td>Your name, role, email, phone, organisation details, the wards you work in and how you'd like to help</td><td>To assess and set up a partnership and to contact you about it</td><td>Legitimate interests, and consent to contact you</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Send a contact form message</td><td>Your name, email, phone (optional), topic and message</td><td>To answer your enquiry</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Use the ward checker or map</td><td>Nothing. The ward you choose stays in your browser and isn't sent to us</td><td>Not applicable</td><td>Not applicable</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p>Please don't include health or other sensitive details in a message unless you need us to know them to help you.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We don't sell your information or use it for marketing. We only share it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>with service providers who host this website and store form responses for us, under contracts that protect your data</li>
        <li>with a partner organisation, such as a local hub, when you have asked us to connect you</li>
        <li>when the law requires us to</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Contact form messages:</b> 2 years after we last reply to you</li>
        <li><b>Partner questionnaires:</b> for as long as you are a partner, then 2 years. If we don't go ahead, 12 months.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask for a copy of the information we hold about you</li>
        <li>ask us to correct information that's wrong</li>
        <li>ask us to delete your information</li>
        <li>object to or ask us to limit how we use it</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on consent</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To use any of these rights, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>. We'll reply within one month.</p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you're unhappy with how we've handled your information, please tell us first. You can also complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner's Office</a> (0303 123 1113).</p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>We'll update this notice if we change how we use personal information. The date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
    </article>
  </div></section>

</Base>
